1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,393
Welcome.

2
00:00:00,393 --> 00:00:06,679
This is the UK Landlord M T D-Ready Bookkeeping
Ledger, version one point zero point one.

3
00:00:06,679 --> 00:00:11,420
It is a local-first Microsoft Excel workbook
for organising property income and expenses,

4
00:00:11,420 --> 00:00:16,107
checking the records, and preparing cumulative
figures for compatible bridging software.

5
00:00:16,107 --> 00:00:22,000
It does not submit directly to H
M R C or calculate your tax bill.

6
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:26,520
The workbook follows one clear routine.

7
00:00:26,520 --> 00:00:30,612
Start here, complete Setup,
record transactions, correct any

8
00:00:30,612 --> 00:00:34,500
warnings, and then review the summaries and M T D Export.

9
00:00:34,500 --> 00:00:37,020
White cells are for your input.

10
00:00:37,020 --> 00:00:38,700
Protected areas contain formulas.

11
00:00:38,700 --> 00:00:45,000
The aim is to keep every reported figure
traceable to the transaction that created it.

12
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:54,192
On Setup, choose the tax year, Standard or Calendar
update periods, and Simple or Full reporting detail.

13
00:00:54,192 --> 00:01:00,538
Then give each property a clear nickname and
leave properties you currently use marked Active.

14
00:01:00,538 --> 00:01:05,615
For jointly owned property, enter transaction
amounts that already represent your share.

15
00:01:05,615 --> 00:01:09,000
The ownership percentage does
not adjust figures automatically.

16
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:16,018
Simple and Full modes control the categories
available in the transaction dropdown.

17
00:01:16,018 --> 00:01:20,618
Simple Mode uses a smaller group
of income and expense categories.

18
00:01:20,618 --> 00:01:23,545
Full Mode provides more detailed reporting categories.

19
00:01:23,545 --> 00:01:26,473
Select the approach appropriate to your circumstances.

20
00:01:26,473 --> 00:01:30,165
The workbook provides the structure, but it does not

21
00:01:30,165 --> 00:01:34,000
decide whether a reporting option is suitable for you.

22
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:38,940
Your update-period choice controls the valid dates.

23
00:01:38,940 --> 00:01:43,980
Standard periods begin on the sixth
of April, July, October and January.

24
00:01:43,980 --> 00:01:49,020
Calendar periods begin on the first
of April, July, October and January.

25
00:01:49,020 --> 00:01:53,187
Once selected, the workbook
validates each transaction date

26
00:01:53,187 --> 00:01:57,000
and assigns it to the correct one of the four periods.

27
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:01,379
Use Transactions for the source records.

28
00:02:01,379 --> 00:02:04,895
Enter the date, an active property, Income or Expense, a

29
00:02:04,895 --> 00:02:08,914
permitted category, a useful
description, and a positive amount.

30
00:02:08,914 --> 00:02:14,069
Add a receipt reference when it helps
connect the row to supporting evidence.

31
00:02:14,069 --> 00:02:18,828
Expenses are entered as positive values
and are kept separate from income.

32
00:02:18,828 --> 00:02:22,000
Do not type over the protected system columns.

33
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:27,600
Warnings tell you that a source row needs attention.

34
00:02:27,600 --> 00:02:31,532
Missing amounts, dates outside the
selected range, inactive properties,

35
00:02:31,532 --> 00:02:34,800
or invalid types and categories
can block export readiness.

36
00:02:34,800 --> 00:02:38,800
Return to the original row, correct it, and check again.

37
00:02:38,800 --> 00:02:42,339
Duplicate receipt references are review warnings, but they

38
00:02:42,339 --> 00:02:46,000
do not by themselves prevent
the export from becoming ready.

39
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:51,833
The quarterly summary shows
standalone activity for each period,

40
00:02:51,833 --> 00:02:55,846
including income, expenses,
transaction counts and invalid records.

41
00:02:55,846 --> 00:03:02,308
The annual summary gives a full-year bookkeeping
overview, together with category and property totals.

42
00:03:02,308 --> 00:03:06,462
Use both pages to spot values that look unexpected.

43
00:03:06,462 --> 00:03:12,000
These are bookkeeping checks, not
calculations of taxable profit or tax due.

44
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:16,966
M T D Export presents cumulative figures.

45
00:03:16,966 --> 00:03:19,085
Update one contains period one.

46
00:03:19,085 --> 00:03:22,051
Update two includes periods one and two.

47
00:03:22,051 --> 00:03:28,831
Update three includes the first three periods, and
update four covers the full selected update year.

48
00:03:28,831 --> 00:03:33,194
Confirm that readiness shows ready,
review the setup and totals, then

49
00:03:33,194 --> 00:03:37,305
follow the process provided by
your compatible bridging software.

50
00:03:37,305 --> 00:03:39,000
Keep a backup first.

51
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:44,574
Version one supports one thousand
preformatted transaction rows.

52
00:03:44,574 --> 00:03:47,702
Automatic expansion beyond that is not supported.

53
00:03:47,702 --> 00:03:54,404
Version one point zero point one has been
tested in Microsoft 365 Excel for Windows.

54
00:03:54,404 --> 00:03:58,348
Compatibility with Excel for Mac and Excel 2021 is not

55
00:03:58,348 --> 00:04:02,000
claimed until those environments have been tested.

56
00:04:04,000 --> 00:04:05,680
The workbook is local-first.

57
00:04:05,680 --> 00:04:10,144
It contains no macros, telemetry,
analytics, hidden web requests or built-in

58
00:04:10,144 --> 00:04:14,080
cloud synchronisation, and no
monthly software account is required.

59
00:04:14,080 --> 00:04:19,471
You decide where the file is stored, how
it is backed up, and when information

60
00:04:19,471 --> 00:04:25,000
is transmitted to another service, including
cloud storage or bridging software.

61
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:29,091
That is the complete workflow.

62
00:04:29,091 --> 00:04:33,096
Set it up, record transactions
consistently, correct warnings,

63
00:04:33,096 --> 00:04:37,036
review the summaries, and check
M T D Export before bridging.

64
00:04:37,036 --> 00:04:42,891
Keep within the documented one thousand rows
and use Microsoft 365 Excel for Windows.

65
00:04:42,891 --> 00:04:50,000
The result is a calmer bookkeeping process with clear
boundaries and figures that remain easy to trace.
